course: dictionary
lesson: 8218
title: Reusable and single-use
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can give you clues. Re- often means "again", so reuse means use again. Add -able, which means "can be", and you get reusable: able to be used again and again. A reusable bag is one you can take shopping many times instead of throwing it away.
explain: Words can be built from parts. Read the word, split off the parts you know, then put the meaning together: re- (again) + use + -able (can be) = can be used again. Try it on «reusable bottle»: a bottle you can fill and drink from many times.
explain: «The order is reduce first, reuse second and recycle third, because recycling still uses energy; a reusable bottle can replace hundreds of throwaway ones.» Here reusable is the opposite of throwaway. Throwaway things are used once and then binned, while reusable things go back into use.
fact: Reusable means able to be used again, many times, instead of being thrown away.
fact: «Reusable» is built from «reuse» plus the ending «-able», which means «can be».
fact: The opposite of reusable is single-use: things like plastic bags or paper cups that are thrown away after one use.
fact: «Reduce, reuse, recycle»: reduce means use less, reuse means use again, and recycle means turn old things into new ones.
fact: Recycling still uses energy, which is why the text puts reusing before recycling.
exercise: What does reusable mean? | Thrown away after one use | Made of plastic | *Able to be used again, many times | Very, very big
exercise: The text says «a reusable bottle can replace hundreds of throwaway ones». What is the opposite of reusable here? | Heavy | *Throwaway | Clean
exercise: Which is a single-use item? | A reusable lunchbox | *A paper cup you use once and throw away | A cloth bag you take shopping every week | A glass jar you wash and fill again
test: In «reduce, reuse, recycle», which word comes second? | Throwaway | Reduce | *Reuse | Recycle
test: Why is a reusable bag better for the planet than a single-use bag? | It is a different colour | *You can use it many times instead of throwing it away | It looks nicer in the shop
exam: Which is a reusable thing? | A paper plate for one picnic | A paper straw used once at lunch | A plastic bag you throw away after one shop | *A metal water bottle you fill again and again
